===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[cause#Verb|Causing]], or [[likely]] to cause, an [[uproar#Noun|uproar]].
# [[characterize|Characterized]] by uproar, that is, [[loud]], [[confused#Adjective|confused]] [[noise#Noun|noise]], or by [[noisy]] and [[uncontrollable]] [[laughter]].
#: {{synonyms|en|uproarish|Thesaurus:noisy}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Christmas Carol|pages=68–69|pageref=68|passage=The noise in this room was perfectly tumultuous, {{...}} every child was conducting itself like forty. The consequences were '''uproarious''' beyond belief; but no one seemed to care; on the contrary, the mother and daughter laughed heartily, and enjoyed it very much; and the latter, soon beginning to mingle in the sports, got pillaged by the young brigands most ruthlessly.}}
#* {{RQ:Northup Twelve Years|chapter=XV|page=219|passage=One "set" off, another takes its place, he or she remaining longest on the floor receiving the most '''uproarious''' commendation, and so the dancing continues until broad daylight. It does not cease with the sound of the fiddle, but in that case they set up a music peculiar to themselves.}}
#* {{RQ:Ruth Thompson Royal Book of Oz|chapter=Dorothy and Sir Hokus Come to Fix City|page=165|passage=The two bushes looked up in surprise, and when they saw Dorothy, the Cowardly Lion and Sir Hokus, they fell into each other's branches and burst into the most '''uproarious''' laughter.}}
#* {{RQ:Orczy Triumph of the Scarlet Pimpernel|chapter=One Crowded Hour of Glorious Life|section=1|page=62|passage=At the '''uproarious''' cheering which greeted his appearance, [[w:Maximilien Robespierre|[Maximilien] Robespierre]] advanced into the open, whilst a sudden swift light of triumph darted from his narrow, pale eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} [[extremely|Extremely]] [[funny#Adjective|funny]]; [[hilarious]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:funny}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=A. A. Dowd|title=''[[w:Good Boys (film)|Good Boys]]'' Puts a Tween Spin on the R-rated Teen Comedy, to Mostly Funny Effect|work={{w|The A.V. Club}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210304011128/https://film.avclub.com/good-boys-puts-a-tween-spin-on-the-r-rated-teen-comedy-1837252319|archivedate=4 March 2021|date=14 August 2019|passage=Yet as with ''{{w|Booksmart}}'', the summer's earlier riff on that Apatovian classic, there are times when ''Good Boys'' feels a little too nice to actually be '''uproarious'''. In more ways than one, it's the training wheels for a better comedy—a slightly edgier and funnier one.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} In a [[mess#Noun|mess]]; [[dishevelled#Adjective|dishevelled]], [[untidy]].

